1
00:06:21,176 --> 00:06:27,176
Goodnight, Mister Tom is a drama, history, war film directed by Jack Gold.

2
00:12:42,352 --> 00:12:48,352
A shy and quiet World War II evacuee is housed by a disgruntled
old man, and they soon develop a close bond.

3
00:19:03,529 --> 00:19:09,529
Tom Oakley, played by John Thaw.

4
00:25:24,705 --> 00:25:30,705
William Beech, played by Nick Robinson.

5
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Mrs. Beech, played by Annabelle Apsion.

6
00:38:07,058 --> 00:38:13,058
Zacharias Wrench, played by Thomas Orange.

7
00:44:28,235 --> 00:44:34,235
Dr. Stelton, played by William Armstrong.

8
00:50:49,411 --> 00:50:55,411
Vicar, played by Geoffrey Beevers.

9
00:57:10,588 --> 00:57:16,588
Goodnight Mister Tom is a 1998 British film adaptation by Carlton
Television of the novel of the same name by Michelle Magorian.

10
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
The film is set during World War II and is about a young evacuee named William Beech who is placed in the care of a reclusive
widower, Tom Oakley, in a rural English village, where he gradually finds love and healing after escaping an abusive home.

11
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
It was Jack Gold's final film as a director.

12
01:16:14,117 --> 01:16:20,117
The cast featured well-known British actors, including veteran actor John Thaw,
who played a bearded character for the first time in his career.

13
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
Filming took place during April and May 1998 in the village of
Turville, chosen due to practical and aesthetic reasons.

14
01:28:56,470 --> 01:29:02,470
Critical reviews were mixed, with critics finding the story and conclusion of the film
predictable, although with praise for the cast performances, particularly Thaw.

15
01:35:17,647 --> 01:35:23,647
The film explores themes of london, england, world war ii,
evacuation, based on children's book, dog.

16
01:41:38,823 --> 01:41:44,823
The tone is emotional.
